  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN-UK Economic Integration Programme (EIP) - Regulatory Reform Inception Phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Office of Product Safety and Standards (OPSS) in DBT are responsible for delivering the inception phase of the Regulatory Reform pillar under the ASEAN Economic Integration Programme. This will be consistent with the attached &#x2018;Proposal: Design and Scoping of the Regulatory Reform Pillar&#x2019; within the EIP Business Case. By the end of the Regulatory Reform pillar inception phase, OPSS will have:
- Presented a viable four year work plan for the pillar to the EIP programme board
- Achieved ASEAN accreditation for the pillar and ASEAN agreement for projects to be delivered in 2024/25
- Secured staff or external supplier(s) to deliver projects that fit with the EIP theory of change</narrative>
  </description>
